Approach: Use slow and fast pointers to find the middle node, while keeping a prev pointer to track the node before slow. Once the middle is found, remove it by linking prev.next to slow.next.

Time Complexity: O(n) — the linked list is traversed only once using two pointers.

Space Complexity: O(1) — only pointer variables are used, no extra data structures.

class Solution {
    public ListNode deleteMiddle(ListNode head) {
        ListNode slow=head,fast=head,prev=head;
        if(head.next==null){
            head=null;
            return head;
        }
        while(fast!=null && fast.next!=null){
            prev=slow;
            slow=slow.next;
            fast=fast.next.next;
        }
        prev.next=slow.next;
        return head;
    }
}
